cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "TensorPyPy: MetaTensor and the MOTION leave transition"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Izawa
    given-names: Yusuke
    affiliation: Tokyo Metropolitan University
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  TensorPyPy is a fork of PyPy whose RPython meta-tracing JIT carries a
  tensor runtime, MetaTensor. Traced chains of tensor operations become fused
  GPU kernels. The repository also holds the MOTION leave transition, which
  is generated from an interpreter change rule, together with an audit of
  that rule and a hand-written adapter for comparison.
keywords:
  - PyPy
  - RPython
  - meta-tracing JIT
  - tensor compiler
  - kernel fusion
  - GPU
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "MetaTensor: Tensor Fusion in a Meta-Tracing Compiler"
